  "agentSummary": "I've recorded all the usages. This is the summary.\n\n- **HeyGen (raw HTTP):** `app/api/heygen-token/route.ts:7` sends `POST https://api.heygen.com/v1/streaming.create_token`. The key comes from `HEYGEN_API_KEY`, and the route returns `data.token` to the client.\n- **HeyGen (`@heygen/streaming-avatar` 2.0.16):** the client is constructed in `useStreamingAvatarSession.ts`. I recorded 19 call sites across the `logic/` hooks and `AvatarChat.tsx`: `createStartAvatar`, `speak`, `startVoiceChat`, `stopAvatar`, mute/unmute, listening and `interrupt`.\n- **OpenAI (raw HTTP):** `app/api/transcribe/route.ts:7` sends `POST /v1/audio/transcriptions`. It passes the client's form data straight through.\n- **OpenAI (`openai` 5.0.1):** the Assistants API (`beta.assistants`, `beta.threads`) is called in `app/api/chat/route.ts` and `app/openai-assistant.ts`. The model is pinned to `gpt-4-turbo-preview`. The class in `app/openai-assistant.ts` runs in the browser with `dangerouslyAllowBrowser`.\n- **LiveKit (`livekit-server-sdk` 2.13.0):** `app/api/livekit/token/route.ts` signs an `AccessToken` JWT locally, so there is no network call. `livekit-client` is in the manifest, but I found no code that uses it.\n- **Unknown backend:** `app/services/api.ts:4` sends `POST ${NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL}/api/v1/ask`. I recorded it as `custom-backend`. It is probably the author's own service, but I couldn't tell from the repo.\n\nThe Pico CSS file loaded from `cdn.jsdelivr.net` in `app/layout.tsx` is a static asset, so I left it out. I didn't open the LiveKit config file `app/config/livekit`. I also didn't confirm that `audio-handler.ts:127` or `AvatarChat.tsx:38` call only the repo's own `/api/*` routes, though the grep output points that way.",
